# Humanize copy

Write like a person talking, not like a changelog or a feature matrix.

## Applies to

Chat replies, README / Thunderstore / store pages, HUD messages, tooltips, hover text, config descriptions, menu labels, notifications, and any other text a player or Sergio will read.

## Do

- Prefer short prose and natural sentences.
- Match the product voice (BlackHearthx = homestead hearth).
- One good table is fine for controls or compat.
- In chat: answer like a colleague — direct, few bullets.

## Don't

- Don't open every line with `-` / `•` when prose would do.
- Don't ship robot lines: "X automatically consumed", "Feature enabled", "Low supply: N remaining".
- Don't use patch-note or agent-notes tone for players.

## Examples

```
Bad:  Cooked meat automatically re-eaten
Good: Had another Cooked meat

Bad:  Low supply: 1 Boar jerky remaining
Good: Last Boar jerky in the bag
```

If it sounds like a manual when read aloud, rewrite it.
